WEBVTT

00:16.435 --> 00:19.335
If my eyes are blinded by the sun

00:19.335 --> 00:24.015
I may just see the limits of the light.

00:24.015 --> 00:25.915
The mind of stardust

00:25.915 --> 00:31.755
What a small universe I live in

00:31.755 --> 00:39.295
Won't somebody give me
a code that starts at zero?

00:39.295 --> 00:41.865
Multiplied and in confusion

00:41.865 --> 00:45.895
A colony dead inside its cage

00:45.895 --> 00:50.375
Shoot your cowardly dreams

00:50.375 --> 00:53.545
Loneliness... self-destruct!

00:53.545 --> 00:57.945
No matter what sacrifices we make

00:57.945 --> 01:01.785
for a future just beyond reach

01:01.785 --> 01:05.455
Let our hearts speak to each other

01:05.455 --> 01:08.755
deep down inside

01:08.755 --> 01:12.895
Though the days just one step behind

01:12.895 --> 01:15.895
will pass even farther from us

01:15.895 --> 01:22.965
You will be in my thoughts

01:54.205 --> 01:56.465
There are two kinds of men.

01:56.465 --> 01:58.505
Men who have their own code of justice...

01:58.505 --> 02:00.305
and men who don't.

02:01.145 --> 02:02.705
A "coliseum"?

02:02.705 --> 02:04.945
It's basically a sports arena.

02:04.945 --> 02:09.685
A place where beastmen knock
human gladiators around for fun.

02:09.685 --> 02:13.015
It's one of the most senseless
forms of entertainment in the world.

02:13.015 --> 02:17.295
W-We're not gonna go try and
tear it down or anything, are we?!

02:17.295 --> 02:19.155
Of course not, silly!

02:19.155 --> 02:22.365
The smart move is to steer clear
of that place and be on our way.

02:22.365 --> 02:23.895
There are even stories
about thugs from the coliseum...

02:23.895 --> 02:29.065
who go around kidnapping humans and forcing
them to be gladiators against their will.

02:33.475 --> 02:35.305
Morte?

02:35.305 --> 02:39.145
This is what we get for telling stories.

02:39.145 --> 02:40.515
Huh?!

02:40.515 --> 02:42.205
Show yourself.

02:47.685 --> 02:49.685
Oh, it's just Toppy!

02:49.685 --> 02:51.495
Don't scare us like that.

02:51.495 --> 02:53.055
So how many'd you catch?

02:53.055 --> 02:54.895
I'm guessing not a single fi...

03:16.885 --> 03:21.755
"There are Two Kinds of Men"

03:21.955 --> 03:27.425
Yeah! Yeah! Woo-hoo!

03:27.425 --> 03:29.295
Get 'im!

03:52.885 --> 03:55.285
Oh no... tell me we're not!

03:55.285 --> 03:57.595
Inside the coliseum.

03:57.595 --> 04:00.595
But how'd we get here?!

04:00.595 --> 04:03.125
That Little Bear and his thugs.

04:03.125 --> 04:05.295
They got the best of me.

04:05.295 --> 04:08.835
"Little Bear"...you mean
from the same tribe as Toppy?

04:08.835 --> 04:11.635
So then, that wasn't Toppy?!

04:12.335 --> 04:15.075
It's the moment you've all been waiting for!

04:15.075 --> 04:17.175
Our next contestants come
courtesy of the horse emperor of Dart...

04:17.175 --> 04:20.575
So give it up for the Horse Team!

04:32.525 --> 04:34.355
Kyrie!

04:36.365 --> 04:37.795
Put it on.

04:37.795 --> 04:39.595
It's basically just for show, though...

04:46.775 --> 04:48.605
Hey, new guys! You're up.

04:48.605 --> 04:51.275
And try to get your butt kicked
in style before you come back.

04:51.275 --> 04:52.845
You want us out there?!

04:52.845 --> 04:54.045
Time to give up hope.

04:54.045 --> 04:56.285
The only way you humans
ever get out of this place...

04:56.285 --> 04:58.715
is in a body bag, if you catch my drift.

04:58.715 --> 05:01.485
No need to be so... dramatic...

05:01.485 --> 05:03.495
Morte!

05:03.495 --> 05:05.325
Calm yourself!

05:05.325 --> 05:09.065
It's just horses... the worst
they can do is snort on us.

05:09.065 --> 05:11.635
It'll work out one way or another.

05:11.635 --> 05:15.135
That's easy for you to say...

05:15.135 --> 05:19.865
Toppy! Where are you when we really need you?!

05:21.175 --> 05:23.745
Can't say I've seen 'em.

05:23.745 --> 05:28.305
Listen buddy, two humans
together? Look around.

05:30.585 --> 05:33.085
That's a pretty common sight 'round these parts.

05:33.085 --> 05:35.915
I see... sorry to bother you, bear-o.

05:39.395 --> 05:41.095
No!

05:41.095 --> 05:43.825
Lookee here... poor girlie
fell down on the gwound.

05:46.565 --> 05:48.665
No!

05:48.665 --> 05:51.235
Let go of that girl's arm, bear-o.

05:51.235 --> 05:53.005
Eh?!

05:53.005 --> 05:54.675
Was that you?!

05:54.675 --> 05:56.435
Down here, bear-o.

06:00.185 --> 06:02.915
Now let go of that girl's arm, bear-o.

06:02.915 --> 06:04.905
You talkin' fresh?!

06:09.355 --> 06:12.625
Say miss, are you hurt at all, bear-o?

06:12.625 --> 06:16.065
I'm fine... thank you so much!

06:16.065 --> 06:18.255
You haven't changed a bit, bear.

06:26.705 --> 06:28.105
Yappy!

06:46.655 --> 06:48.925
What's this?! A major upset!

06:48.925 --> 06:50.465
The human has won!

06:50.465 --> 06:54.265
Did the Horse Team make a bad
call on the weight adjustment?!

06:54.265 --> 06:55.635
Is it over?

06:57.635 --> 06:59.765
You're something else...

07:03.645 --> 07:07.515
Both of us went and got old, didn't we bear?

07:07.515 --> 07:11.685
I guess it has been 20 years since
we left the village together, bear-o.

07:11.685 --> 07:13.825
You been doing well all this time, bear-o?

07:13.825 --> 07:15.785
Well as can be expected, bear.

07:15.785 --> 07:17.695
How about you, bear?

07:17.695 --> 07:20.295
Well... same as always, bear-o.

07:20.295 --> 07:23.025
Here you go! Jumbo salmon.

07:23.025 --> 07:25.325
Courtesy of that woman over there.

07:34.205 --> 07:35.645
Rock!

07:35.645 --> 07:36.775
Paper!

07:36.775 --> 07:38.145
- Bear-o!
- Bear!

07:41.385 --> 07:43.945
Sorry, buddy bear-o.

07:45.455 --> 07:48.985
In the old days we used to split our
meals like this all the time, didn't we bear?

07:48.985 --> 07:51.625
We sure did, bear-o.

07:51.625 --> 07:55.065
Now that I think about it, that
time before was just like this, bear-o.

08:00.565 --> 08:04.535
That time when you and me first
vowed we'd be heroes someday.

08:04.535 --> 08:09.375
I'm curious, though... what are
you doing here anyway, bear?

08:09.375 --> 08:12.545
It seems some friends of mine wound
up getting themselves captured, bear-o.

08:12.545 --> 08:15.245
So I came here to save them, bear-o.

08:16.045 --> 08:17.715
"Captured"?

08:17.715 --> 08:20.255
These friends of yours...
you're saying they're human, bear?

08:20.255 --> 08:21.755
Yeah.

08:21.755 --> 08:24.395
Why would you be with humans?

08:24.395 --> 08:26.655
Well... things happen, bear-o.

08:26.655 --> 08:31.835
But we can't just look the other way
when people are in trouble, can we bear-o?

08:31.835 --> 08:33.595
Maybe you've seen them, bear-o.

08:33.595 --> 08:38.095
There's two of them... a bad-tempered girl
and a real submissive-looking guy, bear-o.

08:39.405 --> 08:40.735
Nope.

08:45.845 --> 08:48.015
It was a human, guys.

08:48.015 --> 08:51.385
A once-in-a-blue-moon thing, but hey,
it seems a human's winning the fights right now.

08:51.385 --> 08:52.215
A human?

08:52.215 --> 08:55.425
That's right. From what they say,
it's a ridiculously strong girl...

08:55.425 --> 08:59.725
paired with some ridiculously wimpy
guy who keeps hidin' behind her skirt.

08:59.725 --> 09:00.525
It couldn't be!

09:00.525 --> 09:02.185
Yappy, sir!

09:05.695 --> 09:06.365
Toppy...

09:06.365 --> 09:09.695
Sorry to run, but something just came up, bear.

09:12.605 --> 09:17.775
Say there... what happens to the
gladiators after the fight's over, bear-o?

09:17.775 --> 09:22.415
What happens? Well, the coliseum
doubles as a prison for the gladiators...

09:22.415 --> 09:26.405
so my guess is they'll be locked up in there...
long as they stay alive, anyway.

09:27.255 --> 09:29.485
You take the credit for this one, Yappy ol' boy!

09:29.485 --> 09:32.755
Since those two humans you brought
me started winning their matches...

09:32.755 --> 09:35.225
the fights are more exciting than ever!

09:35.225 --> 09:37.595
Just look!

09:37.595 --> 09:38.835
So what do you think?

09:38.835 --> 09:43.295
Now wouldn't you say you made the right
call giving up all that unpaid hero nonsense?

09:45.005 --> 09:47.675
You don't seriously intend to
keep calling yourself a hero

09:47.675 --> 09:50.345
after going around
kidnapping people, now do you?

09:50.345 --> 09:53.505
You there, go put this in the safe.

10:02.925 --> 10:04.025
Hey!

10:04.025 --> 10:06.085
Who are you...?!

10:14.265 --> 10:16.165
Sorry I'm late, bear-o.

10:16.165 --> 10:18.005
Toppy!

10:18.005 --> 10:20.095
Are you the real one?

10:39.695 --> 10:42.165
You're saying it was a
Little Bear who looked just like me?

10:42.165 --> 10:44.895
Yeah. Someone you know?

10:44.895 --> 10:48.065
No... there's no way it's him, bear-o!

10:57.875 --> 11:00.645
Hey! What was that sound?!

11:02.145 --> 11:03.745
It's a prison break, bear!

11:05.155 --> 11:08.225
Some humans are trying to escape, bear!

11:08.225 --> 11:10.815
Hurry and capture them, bear!

11:11.195 --> 11:13.055
What is this, bear-o?!

11:13.055 --> 11:15.665
Seize that Little Bear too, bear!

11:15.665 --> 11:17.595
He's a friend of those humans, bear!

11:17.595 --> 11:19.235
Yappy!

11:19.235 --> 11:20.895
Kyrie!

11:26.405 --> 11:28.495
Yappy!

11:42.755 --> 11:45.725
You want to make that
Little Bear into a gladiator?!

11:45.725 --> 11:49.765
I don't know... there's never been a case
of a beastman fighting alongside humans.

11:49.765 --> 11:51.635
That's the whole point, bear.

11:51.635 --> 11:54.765
It's once-in-a-lifetime event that
people can get excited about, bear.

11:54.765 --> 11:56.035
All right, then.

11:56.035 --> 11:59.035
When it comes to choosing
opponents, I'll take your word for it.

11:59.035 --> 12:01.075
But you're sure you're okay with this?

12:01.075 --> 12:04.475
Isn't the beastman in
question a compatriot of yours?

12:04.475 --> 12:06.415
He used to be, bear.

12:06.415 --> 12:09.615
At this point, there's
nothing more between us, bear.

12:09.615 --> 12:13.955
Oh, and by the way, I'm glad you were
there to prevent those humans from escaping...

12:13.955 --> 12:18.555
but what were you doing
down there in the first place?

12:18.555 --> 12:22.085
Where I choose to be is
none of your business, bear.

12:24.665 --> 12:26.295
Step right up and place your bets!

12:26.295 --> 12:31.805
It's a coliseum first... beastmen and humans
fighting on the same team as fellow gladiators!

12:31.805 --> 12:33.805
But if the three of us all fight together...

12:33.805 --> 12:36.605
won't someone figure out that
we're the World Destruction Committee?

12:36.605 --> 12:37.975
Well, it's out of our hands now.

12:37.975 --> 12:40.345
But if we get found out
in a seedy place like this...

12:40.345 --> 12:44.485
who knows what all those
reward-hungry citizens might try and do to us.

12:44.485 --> 12:46.975
What does all this mean, bear-o?!

12:48.125 --> 12:49.425
Yappy...

12:49.425 --> 12:51.195
It's just a way of shutting us up.

12:51.195 --> 12:54.465
He plans to kill us...
but he wants to do it legally.

12:54.465 --> 12:56.195
There's no way Yappy'd ever do something like...

12:56.195 --> 12:57.125
Yes he would!

12:57.125 --> 13:00.765
You were there... you saw the
bag he was carrying, didn't you?

13:00.765 --> 13:03.165
He was trying to make
off with a bag of stolen cash,

13:03.165 --> 13:05.335
but as bad luck would have it,
we caught him in the act...

13:05.335 --> 13:07.175
and now we're in the way.

13:07.175 --> 13:08.645
It's as simple as that.

13:08.645 --> 13:10.545
Morte, you don't have to put it like...

13:10.545 --> 13:11.675
It's the truth!

13:11.675 --> 13:15.715
And besides, he was the one who
kidnapped us and threw us in here!

13:15.715 --> 13:18.115
Ambushing us with his gang of thugs!

13:18.115 --> 13:20.515
Maybe he's an old friend
of yours and maybe he's not...

13:20.515 --> 13:22.885
but do you really
want to trust a guy like that?!

13:22.885 --> 13:24.725
Hey, you three!

13:24.725 --> 13:26.655
You're up!

13:33.665 --> 13:37.235
Yappy, are you sure this is the
opponent we should be going with?

13:37.235 --> 13:41.305
It won't be very exciting if the
humans don't win at least a little bit...

13:41.305 --> 13:43.505
It'll be fine, bear.

13:43.505 --> 13:45.175
Yo missy, go get 'em!

13:45.175 --> 13:47.815
Hey, boy-o! Try 'n' do somethin' this time!

13:47.815 --> 13:50.915
And now... it's the
moment you've all been waiting for!

13:50.915 --> 13:53.015
The fight is about to begin!

13:53.015 --> 13:55.325
- Yappy...
- First up, still on their
amazing run of wins!

13:55.325 --> 14:00.865
The two humans, now joined by a
beastman... it's the gladiator dream team!

14:00.865 --> 14:05.265
This time they face off against the worker
of the fields... the one and only sand worm!

14:05.265 --> 14:07.255
Eh?! Where? Where?

14:31.395 --> 14:35.055
Whoa there! An unstoppable
assault from the sand worm!

14:42.935 --> 14:43.925
Whoa!

14:57.245 --> 14:59.785
And what a reversal!

14:59.785 --> 15:04.085
The underdog gladiators take the win!

15:05.625 --> 15:06.425
Toppy!

15:06.425 --> 15:08.725
That was amazing, Toppy!

15:18.635 --> 15:21.675
And now... today we
have a battle series for you!

15:21.675 --> 15:22.805
Their next opponent

15:22.805 --> 15:25.975
has laid countless gladiators to
rest with his powerful death swing!

15:25.975 --> 15:29.285
It's the Minotaur Holstein!

15:29.285 --> 15:31.355
Wait, a battle series?!

15:31.355 --> 15:34.325
Yappy... you're willing
to go this far to do us in?!

15:34.325 --> 15:35.815
He's coming!

15:41.795 --> 15:43.195
No!

15:53.175 --> 15:54.605
Toppy!

16:13.725 --> 16:17.565
Um, hello... my name is Mutton.

16:17.565 --> 16:19.335
A little while ago I was saved by that...

16:19.335 --> 16:21.635
What do you want, bear?

16:21.635 --> 16:25.335
What do you mean?
You're not going to save him?

16:28.975 --> 16:31.735
But aren't you his friend?

16:34.245 --> 16:38.385
Please, I beg you! Please save him!

16:38.385 --> 16:39.585
Why should I?

16:39.585 --> 16:40.855
Huh?

16:40.855 --> 16:44.425
What's so different about him and me, bear?

16:44.425 --> 16:49.265
The truth is... before he stepped in,
I was planning to save you too, bear.

16:49.265 --> 16:52.235
So why then, bear?!

16:52.895 --> 16:56.695
He's not the only... not the only one!

16:57.775 --> 16:59.505
You brute!

16:59.505 --> 17:01.535
Take this!

17:11.685 --> 17:17.025
Toppy... why's it always you?!

17:20.395 --> 17:22.265
Are you hurt, bear-o?

17:22.265 --> 17:25.095
I'm fine. But Toppy, what about you?!

17:25.095 --> 17:27.935
Nothing to be worried about, bear-o.

17:39.775 --> 17:42.445
What the heck does he think he's doing?!

17:42.445 --> 17:47.315
On the other hand...
this may be just too good to pass up!

17:47.315 --> 17:50.375
Hey! Go gather up all
the bets and bring 'em here!

17:51.555 --> 17:53.325
Listen up everybody!

17:53.325 --> 17:57.955
We're in for a rare treat... a grudge
match against two fellow Little Bears!

18:04.905 --> 18:07.975
So you've decided to come
down and kill us off yourself?

18:07.975 --> 18:09.975
Is that what this is, bear-o?!

18:09.975 --> 18:12.775
When we made that pledge
together that we'd be true heroes...

18:12.775 --> 18:15.005
was that just a lie, bear-o?!

18:18.285 --> 18:20.115
Yappy!

18:21.585 --> 18:23.285
Get back, bear-o!

18:47.215 --> 18:50.875
I accidentally killed a
beastman on one of my jobs, bear.

18:51.655 --> 18:54.325
They ran me out of the Hero
Guild and left me to fend for myself.

18:54.325 --> 18:57.995
But the bird took me in and this
has been my life ever since, bear!

18:57.995 --> 19:00.625
You think that's an excuse for
being a kidnapper and a thief, bear-o?!

19:00.625 --> 19:02.655
Don't make me laugh, bear-o!

19:10.005 --> 19:13.535
You've been a hero your whole
life with no problems of any kind.

19:13.535 --> 19:15.305
What do you know about my life?!

19:15.305 --> 19:16.805
Bear!

19:16.805 --> 19:18.365
Bear-o!

19:39.565 --> 19:42.335
What a fight! What an amazing fight!

19:42.335 --> 19:45.925
And the gladiators claim victory!

19:48.745 --> 19:50.765
Look at all this!

19:58.355 --> 20:00.115
Yappy...

20:00.115 --> 20:03.175
How did things ever get this bad, bear-o?

20:06.525 --> 20:08.195
I want mine too!

20:08.195 --> 20:10.025
Something's happened!

20:11.735 --> 20:13.065
What is it?

20:13.065 --> 20:15.765
All the money in the safe... it's gone!

20:15.765 --> 20:17.435
What?!

20:17.435 --> 20:20.235
What do you mean the money's gone?!

20:20.235 --> 20:21.975
I don't have the foggiest...

20:21.975 --> 20:23.245
Now that you mention it...

20:23.245 --> 20:24.735
What is it?!

20:26.045 --> 20:28.585
A little while back I was
walking near the safe...

20:28.585 --> 20:30.115
and I saw someone's shadow.

20:30.115 --> 20:32.615
Someone's shadow?!

20:32.615 --> 20:37.155
Judging from the height...
I thought it might've been a Little Bear.

20:37.155 --> 20:39.385
A Little Bear!

20:40.555 --> 20:45.435
What were you doing
down there in the first place?

20:45.435 --> 20:48.665
Where I choose to be is
none of your business, bear.

20:48.665 --> 20:50.765
I don't believe it!

20:54.605 --> 20:57.745
- What'd he say?
- Somethin' 'bout no money?

20:57.745 --> 20:59.975
Not only am I no hero...

21:01.515 --> 21:05.155
Not only am I no hero, but I've
stooped to the level of kidnapping!

21:05.155 --> 21:08.755
So why should I care about
a little thing like betrayal, bear?!

21:08.755 --> 21:09.285
It was...

21:09.285 --> 21:11.485
It was me, bear-o!

21:14.865 --> 21:16.825
Just who do you think
you're dealing with anyway, bear-o!

21:16.825 --> 21:17.625
Eh?!

21:17.625 --> 21:20.695
I'm Toppy from the
World Destruction Committee, bear-o!

21:20.695 --> 21:22.705
What are you doing?!

21:22.705 --> 21:26.805
I've helped myself to your precious bet money!

21:26.805 --> 21:28.045
What did he say?

21:28.045 --> 21:30.545
Th-Those three!

21:30.545 --> 21:32.615
They're from the World Destruction Committee!

21:32.615 --> 21:35.185
If they're the ones... in the wanted poster!

21:35.185 --> 21:36.645
Reward?

21:36.645 --> 21:42.625
Reward!

21:42.625 --> 21:44.025
Hand it over!

21:44.025 --> 21:45.725
S-Stop it!

21:45.725 --> 21:49.525
The World... Destruction Committee?

21:49.525 --> 21:50.665
Yappy...

21:50.665 --> 21:52.965
It doesn't matter what
circumstances you find yourself in.

21:52.965 --> 21:56.505
All it takes to be a hero is
the will to be a hero, bear-o.

21:56.505 --> 21:58.335
We've gotta run for it! Hurry!

21:58.335 --> 22:00.335
Toppy!

22:00.335 --> 22:02.175
As for me, no matter what happens...

22:02.175 --> 22:05.145
I choose to be a hero, bear-o.

22:21.055 --> 22:24.565
The glimmering seas of sand

22:24.565 --> 22:27.695
The end of the green earth

22:27.695 --> 22:33.775
Memories overflowing from the sky

22:33.775 --> 22:36.905
now plunged into darkness

22:36.905 --> 22:40.115
The memories will pile up

22:40.115 --> 22:46.115
like mounds of rubble

22:46.115 --> 22:49.355
Mutual encounters

22:49.355 --> 22:52.425
Misunderstood feelings

22:52.425 --> 22:55.565
Interwoven words

22:55.565 --> 22:58.695
People hurting each other

22:58.695 --> 23:10.805
Does the path we walk on
still lead us to tomorrow?

23:13.645 --> 23:17.485
Living this moment against the world

23:17.485 --> 23:20.485
isn't just about changing the world

23:20.485 --> 23:26.055
We're off on a distant journey across the waves

23:26.055 --> 23:29.625
So let our living heartbeat echo in the wind

23:29.625 --> 23:33.165
Around the world, to the end of the world

23:33.165 --> 23:39.135
Until we reach

23:39.135 --> 23:50.745
the promised land just beyond

23:52.655 --> 23:56.325
So hot... can't go on...

23:56.325 --> 23:58.695
We made landfall at the summer continent...

23:58.695 --> 24:02.595
but wound up collapsing in the
face of the awesome power of nature.

24:02.595 --> 24:05.365
We were taken to an elephant's hospital,
and what we saw there...

24:05.365 --> 24:07.265
was a vision of peace and tranquility...

24:07.265 --> 24:09.205
where beastmen and humans
lived together in harmony,

24:09.205 --> 24:11.005
and the children ran and
played with smiles on their faces.

24:11.005 --> 24:13.635
Next time on World Destruction... Episode 6:

24:13.635 --> 24:15.475
"There Are Two Kinds of Summers."

24:15.475 --> 24:18.345
Toppy, you're stiflingly hot!

24:18.345 --> 24:20.865
Well, I can't take my coat off!
